TASK SPECIFICATIONS:
{
  "id": "PUB006",
  "title": "Aeration Blower Delayed Start",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "requirements": "# Aeration Blower Delayed Start\n\n- **Difficulty:** Easy (easy)\n\n## Requirements\n\nControl a wastewater-treatment aeration blower with a low-dissolved-oxygen demand, a 5-second start delay, emergency-stop priority and start-cycle counting.\n\n1. Start delay timing when both DO_LOW and AERATION_E_STOP_NC are TRUE. Allow BLOWER_RUN to become TRUE only after these conditions have remained satisfied for 5 seconds.\n2. If DO_LOW becomes FALSE or an emergency stop occurs, immediately disable BLOWER_RUN and reset the start timer, whether timing is incomplete or complete. A new demand must wait the full 5 seconds again.\n3. Increment AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT once on each FALSE-to-TRUE transition of BLOWER_RUN. Do not count repeatedly during continuous operation.\n4. At power-up, initialize the blower to OFF and the start count to zero. The start delay gates a BOOL enable; no continuous speed ramp is required.\n\n## Interface Definition\n\n| Direction | Variable/Field | Data Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Input | `DO_LOW` | `BOOL` | Dissolved oxygen is below its threshold and aeration is needed. |\n| Input | `AERATION_E_STOP_NC` | `BOOL` | TRUE means the emergency stop is inactive; FALSE means it is active. |\n| Output | `BLOWER_RUN` | `BOOL` | Blower motor-contactor run command. |\n| Output | `AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT` | `UINT` | Count of actual blower starts. |",
  "scenario": "Control a wastewater-treatment aeration blower with a low-dissolved-oxygen demand, a 5-second start delay, emergency-stop priority and start-cycle counting.",
  "interface": [
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "DO_LOW",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Dissolved oxygen is below its threshold and aeration is needed."
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "AERATION_E_STOP_NC",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "TRUE means the emergency stop is inactive; FALSE means it is active."
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "BLOWER_RUN",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Blower motor-contactor run command."
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT",
      "type": "UINT",
      "description": "Count of actual blower starts."
    }
  ],
  "initial_conditions": {
    "BLOWER_RUN": false,
    "AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT": 0,
    "delayElapsed_ms": 0
  },
  "scan_semantics": "At scan k, inputs I[k] are sampled once, q[k] is pre-scan retained state, outputs O[k] are observed after execution, and q[k+1] is the updated state. Each test creates a fresh FB instance before step 0. An initialized instance has not yet executed a scan. Timer elapsed time is zero on the first eligible sampled invocation; dt_ms is elapsed wall time since the previous invocation, not automatically a synthetic input to the FB. No unobserved past input stability is assumed. All sequences here are expected values.",
  "safety_priority": [
    "DO_LOW FALSE or emergency stop overrides timing and resets it immediately."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Start delay elapsed is zero at the first sample of DO_LOW & AERATION_E_STOP_NC; run becomes TRUE at elapsed>=5s.",
    "Count increments on the same invocation that changes end-of-scan BLOWER_RUN from FALSE to TRUE.",
    "Tests stay below UINT overflow; overflow behavior is outside the specified operating domain.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values."
  ],
  "ltl": [
    {
      "id": "PUB006.P_init",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "init",
      "description": "Before the first scan invocation, all declared OUTPUT variables and initial instance state hold their declared initial values.",
      "explanation": "Applies strictly to the fresh pre-invocation initial instance observation before scan k=0 (INITIAL_INSTANCE scope).",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "INITIAL_INSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB006.P1",
      "formula": "G(BLOWER_RUN <-> (permit & delayDone))",
      "explanation": "Run is enabled only after the full delay.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB006.P2",
      "formula": "G(!permit -> (!BLOWER_RUN & X(!delayDone)))",
      "explanation": "Loss of demand or safety permissive clears run and its timer.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB006.P3",
      "formula": "G((!runPrev & BLOWER_RUN) -> AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT=countPrev+1)",
      "explanation": "One count per genuine start.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB006.P4",
      "formula": "G((runPrev | !BLOWER_RUN) -> AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT=countPrev)",
      "explanation": "No repeated count during continuous operation or stop.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB006.P5",
      "formula": "(G(F(TimeTick))) -> (G((G(permit)) -> F(BLOWER_RUN)))",
      "explanation": "A sustained permitted demand eventually starts under advancing time. Explicit non-Zeno environment premise: physical elapsed time crosses infinitely many 1ms boundaries.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    }
  ],
  "atomic_propositions": {
    "permit": "DO_LOW & AERATION_E_STOP_NC",
    "delayDone": "Permissive has continuously remained true for >=5s after its first sampled TRUE.",
    "runPrev": "{\"kind\": \"previous_observed_output\", \"source\": \"O[k-1].BLOWER_RUN\", \"initial\": false, \"update\": \"After comparing scan k, store ACTUAL O[k].BLOWER_RUN; never write into reference state.\"}",
    "countPrev": "{\"kind\": \"previous_observed_output\", \"source\": \"O[k-1].AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT\", \"initial\": 0, \"update\": \"After comparing scan k, store ACTUAL O[k].AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT; never write into reference state.\"}",
    "interface names": "Identically named sampled input or observed output.",
    "TimeTick": "Boolean: floor(t[k]/1ms)>floor(t[k-1]/1ms), with t[0]=0, TimeTick[0]=FALSE, t[k]=sum(dt_ms[1..k]). G(F(TimeTick)) states unbounded physical time progress; merely positive dt is insufficient.",
    "DO_LOW": "I[k].DO_LOW: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "AERATION_E_STOP_NC": "I[k].AERATION_E_STOP_NC: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "BLOWER_RUN": "O[k].BLOWER_RUN: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT": "O[k].AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT: independently observed post-scan candidate value (UINT); never defined as expected output.",
    "init": "At the separate pre-invocation initial observation before scan k=0: O_init.BLOWER_RUN=false, O_init.AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT=0."
  }
}

ARCHITECTURAL PLAN:
{
  "state_machine": {
    "initial_state": "IDLE",
    "states": [
      {
        "name": "IDLE",
        "description": "Blower OFF. Start timer reset whenever permit is FALSE. Waiting for a valid demand and safety permissive.",
        "actions": [
          "BLOWER_RUN remains FALSE through final output stage",
          "No cycle count increment"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "DELAY",
        "description": "Valid demand exists: DO_LOW = TRUE and AERATION_E_STOP_NC = TRUE. Start-delay timer is accumulating. Blower remains OFF until 5 s has elapsed.",
        "actions": [
          "StartDelayTON.IN = permit",
          "BLOWER_RUN remains FALSE until StartDelayTON.Q = TRUE"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "RUN",
        "description": "Delayed start complete and permissive still TRUE. Blower run command is enabled through the output stage.",
        "actions": [
          "BLOWER_RUN remains TRUE only while permit remains TRUE",
          "Cycle count increments only on FALSE-to-TRUE edge of BLOWER_RUN"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "transitions": [
      {
        "from": "IDLE",
        "to": "DELAY",
        "condition": "DO_LOW = TRUE AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC = TRUE",
        "priority": "normal"
      },
      {
        "from": "IDLE",
        "to": "IDLE",
        "condition": "DO_LOW = FALSE OR AERATION_E_STOP_NC = FALSE",
        "priority": "safety-hold"
      },
      {
        "from": "DELAY",
        "to": "RUN",
        "condition": "DO_LOW = TRUE AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC = TRUE AND StartDelayTON.Q = TRUE",
        "priority": "normal",
        "note": "The final output stage also uses the post-call StartDelayTON.Q so BLOWER_RUN can assert on the same scan the 5 s delay is reached."
      },
      {
        "from": "DELAY",
        "to": "IDLE",
        "condition": "DO_LOW = FALSE OR AERATION_E_STOP_NC = FALSE",
        "priority": "safety-reset",
        "actions": [
          "Force BLOWER_RUN = FALSE",
          "Reset StartDelayTON"
        ]
      },
      {
        "from": "RUN",
        "to": "RUN",
        "condition": "DO_LOW = TRUE AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC = TRUE",
        "priority": "normal-hold"
      },
      {
        "from": "RUN",
        "to": "IDLE",
        "condition": "DO_LOW = FALSE OR AERATION_E_STOP_NC = FALSE",
        "priority": "safety-reset",
        "actions": [
          "Force BLOWER_RUN = FALSE immediately",
          "Reset StartDelayTON",
          "Retain AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "timer_plan": [
    {
      "name": "StartDelayTON",
      "type": "TON",
      "pt": "T#5s",
      "pt_ms": 5000,
      "in_expression": "DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC",
      "q_usage": "Delay-done permissive. BLOWER_RUN may be TRUE only when permit is TRUE and StartDelayTON.Q is TRUE, or while latched in RUN with permit TRUE.",
      "et_usage": "Elapsed time monitor/debug. First eligible sampled invocation starts at 0 ms; Q becomes TRUE when ET >= 5000 ms.",
      "reset_conditions": [
        "DO_LOW = FALSE",
        "AERATION_E_STOP_NC = FALSE",
        "permit = FALSE",
        "Power-up/initialization",
        "Safety-reset transition to IDLE"
      ],
      "non_reset_conditions": [
        "Do not reset solely because state changes from DELAY to RUN while permit remains TRUE; keeping the timer active preserves delay-done while running."
      ],
      "call_constraint": "Call exactly once per scan as an unconditional top-level FB call outside CASE/IF."
    }
  ],
  "priorities": [
    {
      "rank": 1,
      "name": "Emergency stop / safety permissive",
      "rule": "If AERATION_E_STOP_NC = FALSE, force BLOWER_RUN = FALSE immediately, reset StartDelayTON, and block any delayed-start or run transition."
    },
    {
      "rank": 2,
      "name": "Loss of dissolved-oxygen demand",
      "rule": "If DO_LOW = FALSE, force BLOWER_RUN = FALSE immediately, reset StartDelayTON, and require a new full 5 s delay before any future start."
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "name": "Delayed-start gate",
      "rule": "BLOWER_RUN cannot become TRUE until DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC have remained TRUE continuously for 5000 ms."
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "name": "Cycle counting",
      "rule": "Increment AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT only on the FALSE-to-TRUE transition of the final end-of-scan BLOWER_RUN output. Do not count during power-up, while stopped, or during continuous run."
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "name": "Unified output assignment",
      "rule": "Write BLOWER_RUN and AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT only in the final scan stage, after safety override, state logic, and timer execution."
    }
  ],
  "initial_values": {
    "BLOWER_RUN": false,
    "AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT": 0,
    "state": "IDLE",
    "permit": false,
    "runPrev": false,
    "cycleCount": 0,
    "StartDelayTON": {
      "IN": false,
      "PT": "T#5s",
      "ET_ms": 0,
      "Q": false
    },
    "delayElapsed_ms": 0
  },
  "scan_execution_order": [
    {
      "stage": 1,
      "name": "Edge sampling",
      "actions": [
        "Sample inputs once: DO_LOW and AERATION_E_STOP_NC.",
        "Compute permit := DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC.",
        "Sample previous observed blower output for edge detection: runPrev := BLOWER_RUN, where BLOWER_RUN is the pre-scan retained output O[k-1].",
        "Do not update AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT in this stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage": 2,
      "name": "Safety/reset priority and state transitions",
      "actions": [
        "Apply highest-priority safety reset first: if permit = FALSE, force state := IDLE and set runCmd := FALSE.",
        "Otherwise evaluate state transitions: IDLE -> DELAY when permit = TRUE; DELAY -> RUN when permit = TRUE and StartDelayTON.Q = TRUE; DELAY/RUN -> IDLE when permit = FALSE.",
        "State logic may set internal state/run intent but must not write final BLOWER_RUN or AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT outputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage": 3,
      "name": "Unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF",
      "actions": [
        "Call StartDelayTON(IN := permit, PT := T#5s) exactly once per scan.",
        "If permit = FALSE, the TON resets: Q := FALSE and ET := 0 ms.",
        "If permit = TRUE, the TON accumulates elapsed time and sets Q := TRUE when ET >= 5000 ms.",
        "Do not call the timer inside CASE/IF or conditionally."
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage": 4,
      "name": "Unified output assignments",
      "actions": [
        "Compute final run command: runCmd := permit AND ((state = RUN) OR (state = DELAY AND StartDelayTON.Q)); if permit = FALSE then runCmd := FALSE.",
        "If runCmd = TRUE AND runPrev = FALSE then cycleCount := cycleCount + 1.",
        "Assign BLOWER_RUN := runCmd.",
        "Assign AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT := cycleCount.",
        "No other stage writes BLOWER_RUN or AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "formal_assertions": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "formula": "init(BLOWER_RUN=false && AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT=0)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "formula": "G(BLOWER_RUN -> (DO_LOW && AERATION_E_STOP_NC))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "formula": "G(!(DO_LOW && AERATION_E_STOP_NC) -> (!BLOWER_RUN && X(!BLOWER_RUN)))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "formula": "G((!BLOWER_RUN && X(BLOWER_RUN)) -> (X(AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT)=AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT+1))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "formula": "G((BLOWER_RUN && X(BLOWER_RUN)) -> (X(AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT)=AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "formula": "G((BLOWER_RUN && X(!BLOWER_RUN)) -> (X(AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT)=AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT))"
    }
  ]
}

CODESYS DIALECT CARDS:
[
  {
    "id": "ton_timer",
    "title": "Standard IEC TON Timer Block Invocation",
    "body": "// Standard IEC TON timer: MUST invoke unconditionally OUTSIDE CASE/IF every scan!\nVAR\n    timer : TON;\n    runTimer : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n// Control via boolean IN flag (never put timer(...) only inside an IF/CASE arm):\nrunTimer := (state = 1) AND NOT resetCmd;\ntimer(IN := runTimer, PT := T#2s);\nIF timer.Q THEN\n    // Timer expired; timer.ET holds elapsed time\nEND_IF;"
  },
  {
    "id": "case_state_machine",
    "title": "Explicit CASE State Machine Transitions",
    "body": "// 4-Stage Scan Order: 1) Edge sample 2) Reset/priority & CASE state transition\n// 3) Unconditional top-level TON/R_TRIG calls 4) Unified output assignments\nVAR\n    state : INT := 0; // 0=IDLE, 1=RUN, 2=FAULT\nEND_VAR\nIF emergencyStop THEN state := 2; END_IF;\nCASE state OF\n    0: IF startCmd AND NOT fault THEN state := 1; END_IF;\n    1: IF faultCmd THEN state := 2; ELSIF stopCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    2: IF resetCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    ELSE state := 0;\nEND_CASE;\noutActive := (state = 1); // Assign outputs unconditionally from current state"
  }
]
